Q: If ... continue VS If ... elseif A: <p>I find <code>if</code> with an empty body a bit ugly in code (which to be fair may just be personal preference) but in a more objective perspective <code>if (filter) { continue; }</code> communicates intent better I think. However I do think the filters with <code>continue</code> should be placed at the start of the loop otherwise it does make code harder to follow if it seemingly jumps randomly from the middle of the iteration code.</p>
<p>I do think (in the example code) that</p>
<pre><code>if (item.is_valid &amp;&amp; item.cnt &gt; 0 &amp;&amp; item.freq &gt;= min) { 
    Process(item);
}
</code></pre>
<p>may be better (if it is possible to be used this way)</p>
<p>There is also the option of pre-filtering the iterable and removing the need for this completely</p>

Q: link to remove `#` from url without reloading the page A: <p>This solved:</p>
<pre class="lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:history.pushState(null,null,' ')&quot;&gt;clear hash&lt;/a&gt;
</code></pre>

Q: Custom colors in LineMark? A: <p>yes it is possible to use your custom colours, add this to your Chart</p>
<pre><code>Chart {
...
}
.chartForegroundStyleScale(domain: parts.map(\.name), range: parts.map(\.color))
</code></pre>
